<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has output"@en .
_:N99fac8a8f774453a86ed9cc9bd7da3f0 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#onProperty> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#consistsOf> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.1. Only process operators may be decomposed; states are not decomposed (Part 1, Section 2).\n\nThe defined class axiom follows the VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University: anything with an input and an output that is contained in a process is a process operator. Anything with an input and an output alone may also be a process."@en .
_:N703e8c95763440139ad0c6984043a66f <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#AnnotationProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isWithin> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemLimit> .
_:N0411174618f04b1a9cbe40f5233c68e2 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
_:N8da919477605451db2ce1e6b25a5991c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#nil> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSubProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to the process describing its decomposition. Inferred, not modelled."@en .
_:N7fc8093e3f124366b8d1f7780280c2c0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#rest> _:N7646cbae4d5a415c868aa99978bb3f67 .
_:Nd502d76f94ae48629759d588bb8db2d0 <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#List> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#AlternativeFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.2.2 models alternative process runs as separate flows, again without additional graphical elements. Introducing a class for the alternative flow is a design decision of this pattern. Where alternative flows are present, the system limit must not be used as a balance limit."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Process> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#TechnicalResource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasStateSource> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "Set by the modelling tool according to the type of the connected element. Carries the chain inferring hasInput."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasOutput> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#propertyChainAxiom> _:Nfe084dcf75be49fab275be6307c465fa .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasTarget> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> _:N8dfc1f702c264464b2cedf943eca9218 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Characteristic> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 2, Section 5.2 and Figures 5 to 7.\n\nThe standard fixes this three-part structure but does not prescribe a vocabulary of properties. The entries shown in its figures, such as setpoint value or validity limits, are examples closed by an open placeholder. Non-functional properties of resources therefore have to draw their vocabulary from a further standard."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Energy> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Product> .
_:N90084c21f0d4477999594d511797436c <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#longName> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#State> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 2, Figure 2 carries state as a class of the information model. Part 1, Section 4.1 deliberately avoids the term in the graphical notation because it is considered ambiguous there, and works with product, energy and information directly. This pattern follows Part 2."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasPredecessor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to a process operator preceding it. Inferred, not modelled."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Figure 3 lists the flow as one of the eight symbols of the graphical notation, where it is an edge rather than an object.\n\nReifying the flow as a class is a design decision of this pattern and deviates from the VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University, which models flows as object properties. A reified flow can be identified, annotated and marked as parallel or alternative, none of which an edge can carry.\n\nThe direct properties hasInput and hasOutput are retained and inferred from the reified flows through property chains, so that reasoning over predecessor and successor is unaffected by the reification."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasPredecessor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasAssignment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "has assignment"@en .
_:N9342d5e9100d48c1beff854db68a0ee1 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#intersectionOf> _:N06d208d3459a4b329fe821907fed3baf .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#isComposedOf> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Attribute> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Flow> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ParallelFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Section 4.2.1 recommends modelling parallel process runs as a partially shared flow and explicitly requires no additional graphical elements for them. Introducing a class for the parallel flow is therefore a design decision of this pattern rather than an adoption from the standard.\n\nA parallel flow states that a single connection belongs to a concurrent run. Grouping several connections into one conjunction is expressed through the dependency property between the states involved."@en .
<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Datatype> .
_:N3f21523c373a4e90a633e8aacc667a9c <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#someValuesFrom> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Process> .
_:Nb25677ba61e749558058d9c393992b96 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#unionOf> _:N528ce667f935476dba3cd512e7a320b4 .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#longName> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "long name"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#SystemLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "System Limit"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Normative basis: VDI/VDE 3682 Part 1 and Part 2, issue May 2015.\n\nRelation to prior work: this pattern is built independently but adopts several design decisions from the VDI 3682 ODP of the Institute of Automation Technology at Helmut Schmidt University (https://github.com/hsu-aut/IndustrialStandard-ODP-VDI3682, MIT licence). Adopted are the property chains for predecessor, successor, sub process and upper process, the defined class axiom for ProcessOperator, the dependency property expressing conjunction between states under the open world assumption, and the attribute structure of Identification and Characteristic.\n\nStructural deviations from that pattern are deliberate and documented at the affected elements: flows are reified as classes rather than expressed as object properties, assignments are reified as classes, and the system limit carries an explicit containment relation. See the notes on Flow, Assignment and SystemLimit."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasInput> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Relates a process operator to a state entering it. Inferred from the reified flows, not modelled directly."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#Assignment> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "VDI 3682 Part 1, Figure 3 carries this relation as the usage symbol, an edge of the graphical notation.\n\nReifying the assignment as a class is a design decision of this pattern, taken for the same reasons as the reification of the flow. The VDI 3682 ODP of Helmut Schmidt University models it as the object property isAssignedTo."@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ParallelFlow> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Parallel Flow"@en .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasOperatorSource> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subPropertyOf> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasSource> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#hasPredecessor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/vdi3682#ProcessOperator> .
